The Datatype Ontology
---------------------

src/datatype/schema/datatype.yaml, src/datatype/datamodel/ and project/
render the Datatype Ontology ("Datatypes",
http://linked.data.gov.au/def/datatype), created by Simon J.D. Cox of
CSIRO and published by the Australian Government Linked Data Working
Group (AGLDWG) at https://github.com/AGLDWG/datatype-ont. They are this
project's adaptation of that work: it is rendered as a LinkML schema, and
the schema adds the rules and names its comments mark as its own. They are
not the AGLDWG's or CSIRO's, and their use does not imply endorsement by
either. Each class and property keeps the ontology's IRI, and its
description is the ontology's skos:definition of that term.

upstream/ holds a copy of rdf/datatype.ttl and LICENSE, retrieved from
https://github.com/AGLDWG/datatype-ont/tree/dd8f24120cd59f686086f58175de37807c569e18
(the head of the master branch, 4 June 2021). Each file is identical to
its counterpart there, and scripts/check_upstream_release.py checks that
they stay so. Nothing in this repository changes the copied files.

The two files state different licences (read on 2026-10-31). The
ontology's own dcterms:license, in rdf/datatype.ttl and its HTML page, is
CC0 1.0 (http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). The
repository's LICENSE, added on 4 June 2021, after the ontology's last
change on 3 October 2019, is the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International licence (CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This repository follows
the stricter of the two: this notice gives the attribution CC BY 4.0
asks for, names the licence, links to the material and says what was
changed. Under either licence the material is provided as is, without
warranties.

